    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "theme.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add one arm to decode_channels for a length of 4. The order is alpha, red, green, blue, the same order as the length 8 arm. Each nibble uses hex_digits of one byte times 0x1111, the same scale as the length 3 arm. Do not change the arms for lengths 12, 9, 8, 6, or 3. Do not touch parse_hex_color, high_byte, or hex_value. Do not nest an if inside an if. The existing test bad_color_is_an_error_not_black stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_four_digit_color_keeps_the_alpha uses the helper editor_color_theme with BackgroundColor #8fff. editor_color of BackgroundColor is Some of Rgba(0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0x88). Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Do not add a second case for coherence. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
